\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty steadies, yuan talk stays. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,015 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1999\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 6 (Reuters) - Poland's zloty steadied on Friday as players drew breath after a scramble to square long positions, but some analysts said a test of basket parity was still on the cards. \par \par \uc2  Ukraine's embattled hryvnia extended its slide, but the Israeli shekel regained much of Thursday's lost ground. The Czech crown marked time, digesting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggestions that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  Tension between \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Taiwan and more China devaluation talk continued to dangle over markets in Asia and beyond, and players across the emerging markets board were also looking to Friday's U.S. jobs data for fresh interest rate clues. \par \par \uc2  The zloty, which touched a 14-week low of 1.84 percent above basket parity on Thursday, ticked up to be quoted around 2.50 percent above parity by 1000 GMT - still some four percentage points below the six-month highs seen less than three weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  "The panic is over, it's stabilised and they're very good levels to buy zloty," said one London-based emerging Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  "The whole market had bought into this long zloty play and everyone wanted to come out at the same time, with the current-account figures coming out and euro/dollar moving." \par \par \uc2  Poor current-account figures on Monday sparked the worst of the zloty selloff this week, which was also fanned by news that the budget deficit was perilously close to the full-year target. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said comments by Polish Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz on Thursday that the country's budget was tight but workable were reassuring. But some said perceptions of a divergence between Balcerowicz and the Economy Ministry over inflation forecasts could continue to weigh on the zloty. \par \par \uc2  Poland's medium-term economic picture is widely seen as favourable, and most analysts and traders predict the zloty will soon bounce to at least four percent above parity, but some see further slippage first. \par \par \uc2  Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would stay quiet ahead of U.S. unemployment data due out at 1230 GMT, traders added. \par \par \uc2  Ukraine's hryvnia continued to turn cartwheels, with indicative screen quotes sliding briefly beyond 5.0 to the dollar before settling back around 4.8, compared with under 4.0 less than three weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The hryvnia dropped out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1999 target corridor of 3.4-4.6 per dollar late on Wednesday, but the government said on Thursday it was confident the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hold within the corridor and no administrative restrictions were planned to support it. \par \par \uc2  The government has blamed a jump in fuel costs for the slide, but dealers and economists point the finger at monetary policy after extra banknotes were printed a few months ago. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness was likely in the run-up to presidential elections on October 30, where moderate incumbent Leonid Kuchma could face a stiff challenge from leftist candidates. \par \par \uc2  The nervous shekel revived slightly, although analysts said jitters remained over policy clashes between \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Jacob Frenkel and Finance Minister Abraham Shohat. \par \par \uc2  "I think this'll blow over, but what concerns us more in Israel is that the scope for interest rate cuts is reduced," said John Orford, economist, Eastern Europe and Middle East at Robert Fleming in London. \par \par \uc2  Asian markets continued to fret over rumours of a Chinese devaluation, which have taken on fresh life recently because of China's weaker trade and growth performance and tension between Beijing and Taipei. \par \par \uc2  Devaluation jitters were cited on Friday as a factor in the Thai baht's slide to its weakest since late April, at 37.67 to the dollar, and the Philippine peso's fall to a five-month low of 38.91 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insisted there had been no change in its yuan policy, and the chairman of the Hong Kong Association of Banks said he saw no sign of, nor any need for a devaluation. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.39   36.41   -0.06%   4.57%\par  Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.23    4.27   -0.78%   4.04%\par  Hungary\tab \tab \tab 2