\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals mixed before U.S. jobs data. \b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1999\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0940 GMT - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed in late afternoon \par \par \uc2  trade, while the yen held its firmer bias but did little else \par \par \uc2  ahead of U.S. jobs data. \par \par \uc2      U.S. non-farm payrolls data is due at 1230 GMT and will be \par \par \uc2  keenly watched for clues on the prospect of a rate rise later \par \par \uc2  this month. A Reuters poll gave an average forecast of a \par \par \uc2  199,400 gain in July, while unemployment was expected to remain \par \par \uc2  steady at 4.3 percent. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won wavered around 1,200 but was firmer \par \par \uc2  after exporters and long-dollar players unloaded dollars. \par \par \uc2      The market was unimpressed by Daewoo's agreement with \par \par \uc2  General Motors to hold talks over a "strategic alliance", as \par \par \uc2  traders had hoped for more concrete restructuring initiatives \par \par \uc2  from the debt-laden chaebol. \par \par \uc2  Daewoo would also be spinning off its construction and \par \par \uc2  shipbuilding divisions, its lead creditor Korea First Bank \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the Commerce, Industry and Energy minister \par \par \uc2  estimates South Korea's economy grew 9.3 percent between the \par \par \uc2  second quarters of 1998 and 1999. \par \par \uc2      He also predicted GDP growth of over six percent in the \par \par \uc2  first half of 1999 from the same period a year ago. \par \par \uc2      *** The chairman of the Hong Kong Association of Banks said \par \par \uc2  he saw no need for a yuan devaluation, and that he had seen no \par \par \uc2  signs of such a change in policy by Beijing. \par \par \uc2      He added that he believed the financial markets had been \par \par \uc2  too sensitive to rumours about a devaluation, which have \par \par \uc2  resurfaced recently due to China's poor trade performance and \par \par \uc2  amid worries over Beijing's row with Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  *** The Indonesian rupiah remained on the softer side of \par \par \uc2  7,000, weighed down by further falls in domestic interest rates \par \par \uc2  and a lack of positive news. \par \par \uc2  The head of an official corruption inquiry into the wealth \par \par \uc2  of former president Suharto said the probe was expected to end \par \par \uc2  by late September after being suspended last month when Suharto \par \par \uc2  suffered a stroke. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Finance Minister Bambang Subianto admitted to \par \par \uc2  irregularities in the recovery of interbank loans extended by \par \par \uc2  Bank Bali to banks which have since failed. \par \par \uc2      He said he would "leave it to IBRA (the Indonesian Bank \par \par \uc2  Restructuring Agency) to do the investigation." \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was also softer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \par \par \uc2  the winning bid for Radanasin Bank might be announced later \par \par \uc2  than originally planned, if the same buyer was chosen to take \par \par \uc2  over Nakornthon Bank Plc. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered had reached an agreement to buy \par \par \uc2  Nakornthon bank in April, but the government reopened the \par \par \uc2  bidding in hopes of attracting a more favourable price. The \par \par \uc2  final winning bid would be announced by September 10. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's foreign reserves stood at $31.9 billion on July \par \par \uc2  30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. The IMF has suggested that Thailand \par \par \uc2  maintain about $32-34 billion in reserves. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar was a good deal firmer ahead of \par \par \uc2  the National Day long weekend, which is expected to bring an \par \par \uc2  upward revision to the official full-year GDP forecast. \par \par \uc2  Second-quarter GDP data is due next week and will give some \par \par \uc2  indication of full-year growth. A Reuters poll has produced an \par \par \uc2  average forecast for second-quarter growth of 4.4 percent \par \par \uc2  compared with the second quarter of 1998. \par \par \uc2      *** The Taiwan dollar made little headway as investors \par \par \uc2  sought the U.S. dollar amid still-tense relations with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  markets recently amid rumours of heightened military action by \par \par \uc2  China. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso was slightly easier after coming \par \par \uc2  off a five-month low in late trade, weighed down by the \par \par \uc2  prospect of a rate hike in the U.S., and by speculation of a \par \par \uc2  yuan devaluation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the Monetary \par \par \uc2  Board had decided to leave overnight interest rates unchanged. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day FRI 06 0921GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7000.00......6961.00.........-0.56% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.67........37.46.........-0.56% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.90........38.73.........-0.44% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6690.......1.6753..........0.38% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.040.......32.050..