\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan Fin Min -3: Fin Markets Affected By China Threats \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 1999\par 13:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's bellwether stock index has declined 11% over the past two weeks since the row with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  erupted, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the New Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The stock market has reacted reasonably" over the last couple of days, said Chiu, speaking before a regional meeting of financial officials in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, the Taiwan Institute for Economic Research (TIER) raised its forecast for the island's economic growth this year to 5.34% from 5.28%. The institute said it was still too early to say if tensions with China would affect economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Only large-scale military maneuvers would have an effect on Taiwan's economic growth this year, said Wu Rong-i, the president of TIER. \par \par \uc2  President Lee Teng-hui recently said that relations with China should be on a "state-to-state" basis, and Beijing responded by saying the comments were tantamount to a declaration of independence. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has since threatened "war and conflict" with Taiwan if the island moves toward independence. \par \par \uc2  -By Kirby Chien; (8862) 2502 2557; kirby.chien@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1151GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7q05mdx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
