\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Weaker yen weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 03:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0120 GMT - The weaker yen took the shine off most regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade as Japanese officials returned from a \par \par \uc2  holiday eager to talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. \par \par \uc2      Their confirmation that the U.S. Federal Reserve had sold \par \par \uc2  yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan overnight also kept traders \par \par \uc2  on their toes for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the lack of any \par \par \uc2  action so far pulled the dollar off early highs. \par \par \uc2  The yen had reached five-week highs against the dollar in \par \par \uc2  New York markets on Monday as the BOJ's failure to step in when \par \par \uc2  the dollar fell below 120 yen encouraged players to push it \par \par \uc2  further. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa took up a familiar refrain \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday, saying his ministry would act to avoid movements \par \par \uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that would hinder Japan's economic \par \par \uc2  recovery. \par \par \uc2  *** The Taiwan dollar was looking quite composed after \par \par \uc2  jumping in late Tuesday trade on the back of the strong yen and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped in repeatedly to \par \par \uc2  shield the local unit from volatility sparked by a row with \par \par \uc2  China over Taiwan's sovereignty status. They said the bank had \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both sides to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it welcomed the Taiwan dollar's \par \par \uc2  rebound, noting that "non-economic factors" disturbing trading \par \par \uc2  had faded. \par \par \uc2  It attributed the unit's sharp rise on Tuesday to an influx \par \par \uc2  of foreign equity funds amid a surge in stock prices in Taiwan \par \par \uc2  and elsewhere in Asia. It declined to confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Taiwan was drifting dangerously towards \par \par \uc2  independence, but the military denied a Hong Kong newspaper \par \par \uc2  report that it had been placed on high alert. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. announced plans overnight to send senior diplomats \par \par \uc2  to Beijing and Taipei this week in a new move to calm tensions \par \par \uc2  over Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan is due to release industrial output and export order \par \par \uc2  figures for June at 0230 GMT. Economists in a Reuters poll \par \par \uc2  predicted on average 8.51 percent growth in Taiwan's industrial \par \par \uc2  output in June, reflecting strong export growth. \par \par \uc2  *** The Indonesian rupiah was still poking around a \par \par \uc2  familiar 6,600-6,700 range, with little reaction to news that \par \par \uc2  the final results from the June 7 poll had been delayed yet \par \par \uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  The General Election Commission set a new deadline of July \par \par \uc2  26 to approve a count finally completed last week and \par \par \uc2  previously due to be announced on July 21. \par \par \uc2  It said smaller parties facing political oblivion appeared \par \par \uc2  likely to mount a formal challenge, which would force the \par \par \uc2  official poll monitor to investigate and take a further week. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian newspapers said on Wednesday reformist \par \par \uc2  politician Amien Rais had proposed nominating Moslem leader \par \par \uc2  Abdurrahman Wahid for the presidency. \par \par \uc2  Rais said nominating Wahid would prevent Indonesia being \par \par \uc2  polarised into rival camps supporting opposition figurehead \par \par \uc2  Megawati Sukarnoputri and President B.J. Habibie. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was unmoved by news that former \par \par \uc2  president Suharto had been admitted to hospital after suffering \par \par \uc2  a mild heart attack. \par \par \uc2  *** The Korean won was looking shaky amid the yen's \par \par \uc2  weakness and dollar buying interest triggered by state-bank \par \par \uc2  purchases which pushed the dollar to a high of 1,200 won on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Korean stocks lost over two percent in early trade as \par \par \uc2  investors grew increasingly concerned about the fate of Daewoo \par \par \uc2  Group and its impact on the market if it failed. \par \par \uc2  Daewoo's creditors agreed on Monday to accept the ailing \par \par \uc2  conglomerate's proposal of 10 trillion won in collateral in \par \par \uc2  return for rolling over 7.0 trillion won in short-term debt \par \par \uc2  maturing in the next nine days. \par \par \uc2      *** The Singapore dollar was also a good deal weaker, \par \par \uc2  heading back towards the 1.70 level on the yen's slide. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day WED 21 0121GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6690.00......6685.00.........-0.07% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.15........37.10.........-0.13% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.40........38.36.........-0.10% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6998.......1.6928.........-0.41% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.2