\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals take heart as yen jumps. \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 03:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0120 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took heart from the \par \par \uc2  yen's jump overnight but the gains were far from spectacular \par \par \uc2  and fell well short of matching the yen's 1.50 percent rise \par \par \uc2  from last night's Asian close. \par \par \uc2      The focus among the majors was on euro/dollar, which was \par \par \uc2  leading dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2      Overall business was fairly light due to the Sea's Day \par \par \uc2  holiday in Japan. \par \par \uc2      *** The Taiwan dollar did not benefit much from the yen's \par \par \uc2  rise, with worries about the \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation offset by the fear \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The bank moved in on Monday offering dollars to major local \par \par \uc2  banks outside the market. \par \par \uc2      *** The won was slightly firmer after recent losses with \par \par \uc2  the stock market easing back after recent gains. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active of late in keeping the won \par \par \uc2  in check for the sake of exports so any won gains will be \par \par \uc2  limited. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah picked up slightly but is still shy of the \par \par \uc2  6,500 level and unlikely to get there until the political \par \par \uc2  picture becomes clearer. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht followed the trend and unlike Korea the \par \par \uc2  authorities appear not to want to gain a competitive edge by \par \par \uc2  engineering a lower baht. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul has rejected an \par \par \uc2  appeal made by a former finance minister for the government to \par \par \uc2  use a cheaper baht to raise exports. \par \par \uc2      "It's no time for arguments. There is only one solution. \par \par \uc2  Cut production costs, raise product quality, create new \par \par \uc2  products, and stop thinking about asking the government to let \par \par \uc2  the baht weaken so as to help sell your products," he said. \par \par \uc2      "Any baht discount would only prompt others to compete by \par \par \uc2  improving their efficiency and quality." \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso picked up with traders waiting for \par \par \uc2  new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenventura's speech later \par \par \uc2  today. \par \par \uc2      He is due to speak at 0400 GMT and the market is expecting \par \par \uc2  some strong policy statements. \par \par \uc2      *** The Sing dollar also picked up with H1 trade data due \par \par \uc2  later today. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day TUE 20 0121GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6666.00......6700.00.........0.51% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.11........37.19.........0.22% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.20........38.32.........0.31% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6993.......1.7038.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.280.......32.330.........0.15% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1188.00......1187.50........-0.04% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....118.55.......120.27.........1.45% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.....