\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly firmer, BOJ impact limited. \b0\par\par\uc2 831 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 10:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0849 - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly firmer as the \par \par \uc2  yen proved resilient despite Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The dollar spiked briefly to 121.30 yen but later slipped \par \par \uc2  as the BOJ action had been widely anticipated following \par \par \uc2  repeated verbal threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the dollar was likely to remain on the \par \par \uc2  defensive due to increasing optimism about a recovery in Japan, \par \par \uc2  the possible emergence of inflationary pressures in the United \par \par \uc2  States and jitters over Latin America. \par \par \uc2  *** The Taiwan dollar firmed amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and growing jitters over the political spat with \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  downside on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said inflows of foreign equity funds should provide \par \par \uc2  some support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but this would be countered by \par \par \uc2  players covering short U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan stood by its decision to abandon the "one China \par \par \uc2  policy", ordering state agencies to promote and explain its \par \par \uc2  view to Beijing and the world. \par \par \uc2      But the Chinese military's daily paper said: "The Chinese \par \par \uc2  government...has never promised to renounce the use of force." \par \par \uc2      In a bid to soothe ruffled financial markets, Taiwan's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sheu Jia-dong stressed that the impact of \par \par \uc2  the row on the markets would be short-lived, and reiterated the \par \par \uc2  government's willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah sagged in thin trade as the market absorbed \par \par \uc2  further falls in local interest rates while keeping an eye on \par \par \uc2  the political scene. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's weekly auction of one-month SBI \par \par \uc2  certificates resulted in a weighted average interest rate of \par \par \uc2  15.86 percent against 17.15 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Tentative results from the June parliamentary elections are \par \par \uc2  due to be released on Thursday evening. The results will then \par \par \uc2  have to be verified by the General Election Commission and the \par \par \uc2  final results are due next Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A military source told Reuters that the armed forces (ABRI) \par \par \uc2  was ready to back presidential hopeful Megawati if she picked \par \par \uc2  ABRI chief General Wiranto as her running mate and \par \par \uc2  vice-presidential candidate. \par \par \uc2  *** The Korean won was barely changed with traders \par \par \uc2  expecting it to be sandwiched in a range between exporter \par \par \uc2  dollar sales and dollar demand from local banks preparing to \par \par \uc2  meet a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan loss provision deadline. \par \par \uc2  Government think tank Korea Development Institute forecast \par \par \uc2  GDP growth of 7.5 percent this year, the highest estimate so \par \par \uc2  far and well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast of 6.8 percent \par \par \uc2  growth. \par \par \uc2  The institute also agreed with Finance Minister Kang \par \par \uc2  Bong-kyun, who said earlier that concerns about the economy \par \par \uc2  overheating were groundless, given last year's 5.8 percent \par \par \uc2  contraction. \par \par \uc2  Kang said there would be no major price increases this \par \par \uc2  year. The annual inflation rate is forecast to reach about two \par \par \uc2  percent this year, following a 7.5 percent rise in 1998. \par \par \uc2  Korean bond yields have been rising recently as the market \par \par \uc2  frets about an interest rate hike, but the government has said \par \par \uc2  it does not plan to raise the overnight rate this month. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso was slightly firmer in line with \par \par \uc2  the general regional trend. \par \par \uc2      The Philippines posted a $509 million trade surplus in the \par \par \uc2  first five months of this year, against a $1.6 billion deficit \par \par \uc2  the year before. In May, the surplus was $214 million, against \par \par \uc2  a $251 million deficit in April and a $209 million deficit last \par \par \uc2  May. \par \par \uc2  May exports were up 13.7 percent on the year and up 17.1 \par \par \uc2  percent from April. Imports slipped 3.5 percent on the year and \par \par \uc2  2.5 percent from April. \par \par \uc2      Analysts expected both exports and imports to pick up over \par \par \uc2  the course of the year. \par \par \uc2      *** Thai exports over the first half of the year grew a \par \par \uc2  preliminary 0.89 percent in dollar terms against the same \par \par \uc2  period last year. \par \par \uc2      The Customs Department said exports totalled $27.16 billion \par \par \uc2  over the first six months of 1999. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day THU 15 0827GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6703.00......6675.00........-0.42% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.08........37.07........-0.03% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.10........38.20.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6980.......1.6985.........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.240.......32.280.........0.12% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1183.00......1183.00.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.73.......121.13.........0.33% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6703.00......2432.00........-63.72% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.09........25.90........-30.17% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.10........26.50........-30.45% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6980.......1.4300........-15.78% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.2400......27.7500........-13.93% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1183.00.......842.00........-28.83% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.73.......114.40.........-5.24% \par \par \uc2      ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7f04fwj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
