\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends steady in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1999\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 1 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed steady against the dollar on Tuesday, as light buying by domestic banks offset selling on concerns over China's slowing exports, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended unchanged at 8.2785 to one dollar in thin trade on the tightly controlled national market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some local banks nibbled at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Beijing has held fast in its policy not to devalue. \par \par \uc2  But other banks were showing renewed signs of nervousness over slowing exports amid concerns over China's prospects for joining the World Trade Organisation (WTO), they said. \par \par \uc2  China's aim to join the WTO this year has been overshadowed by new strains in Sino-U.S. ties, including the NATO bombing of China's embassy in Belgrade and a U.S. congressional report accusing Beijing of stealing American nuclear technology. China has denied the U.S. allegations. \par \par \uc2  Failure to gain admission to the world trade body was widely seen as delaying a recovery in exports and in turn pressuring the yuan. China's exports fell 7.8 percent in the first four months of this year amid Asia's prolonged financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move narrowly in the near future. \par \par \uc2  The yuan touched an intraday high of 8.2780 on Tuesday and a low of 8.2786 with most business done at 8.2784, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2784. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the Japanese yen at 6.7805 to 100 yuan from Monday's 6.8113. It closed slightly higher against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0678 to one dollar from 1.0680. \par \par \uc2     ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv61079ly\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
