\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends steady on Zhu remarks. \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1999\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed steady against the dollar on Thursday, buoyed by Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji's promise the government would keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable "for a long time". \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2778 to one dollar, unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Zhu, who has vowed repeatedly to keep the yuan steady, made his latest statement in a meeting on Wednesday with Joseph Yam, chief of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Zhu's remarks helped stabilise sentiment on the yuan," said a Shanghai-based dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was under pressure after the Federal Open Market Committee, the monetary policy arm of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Tuesday it had shifted its stance from neutral to one that favoured a tightening of credit, implying a possible interest rate rise in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Shanghai had expected the yuan to fall slightly as a result. \par \par \uc2  Trade picked up slightly on Thursday as a result of Zhu's remarks, dealers said. It had remained thin after months of declines in turnover as many domestic banks have been offsetting customer demand internally without using the national market. \par \par \uc2  The market does not post daily trading volumes. \par \par \uc2  Despite the renewed no-devaluation pledge, there was no evidence that the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly-controlled market to support the yuan on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to fall slightly on Friday and move in a narrow range between 8.2780 and 8.2800, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan touched an intraday high of 8.2775 on Thursday and a low of 8.2785 with most business done at 8.2782, they said. \par \par \uc2  It closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.6471 to 100 yen from Wednesday's 6.6909. It closed up slightly against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0670 to one dollar from 1.0672. \par \par \uc2  ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5k00ic8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
