\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan eases, eyes on NATO strains. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 1999\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed easier against the dollar in thin trade on Monday amid concerns over the possible impact of NATO's accidental bombing of China's embassy in Yugoslavia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said technical factors were behind the modest retreat in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and there was no immediate impact from the strike at the embassy in Belgrade. \par \par \uc2  But they added the market was wary of possible repercussions in foreign investment and trade if the latest strains in Sino-U.S. ties persisted. \par \par \uc2  The yuan edged down to 8.2785 against the dollar from Friday's close of 8.2780. \par \par \uc2  "The fall was linked to technical selling," said a dealer at a foreign bank. "The bombing had no immediate impact." \par \par \uc2  China's official media have condemned the United States over the incident while angry students have taken to the streets in protest. \par \par \uc2  China's reaction has raised worries that trade and foreign investment could slow, in turn putting pressure on the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "But the tension in the market was apparent as bank traders kept a watchful eye on the possible impact on trade and foreign investment," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could see a slight downward trend in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly controlled market to boost the yuan on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan hit an intraday high of 8.2784 on Monday and a low of 8.2789 with most business done at 8.2785, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Friday was 8.2783. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up slightly against the Japanese yen at 6.8432 to 100 yen from Friday's 6.8610. \par \par \uc2  It inched up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0673 to one dollar from 1.0675. \par \par \uc2  ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5a01enk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
