\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up, eyes on trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1999\par 06:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed higher against the dollar in thin trade on Friday, buoyed by light buying by local banks on expectations that April exports would show an improvement, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday high of 8.2780 to one dollar from 8.2785 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  China is expected to announce April trade data next week and the market is looking to a recovery in sluggish exports. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations of better foreign trade data triggered bank demand over the past two days," a local bank dealer said. "But the yuan met resistance at the 8.2780 level." \par \par \uc2  The tightly-controlled market has focused its attention on the nation's weakening export position although China has repeatedly said it would not devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Exports were down 7.9 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  "April's trade data will be a key market-moving factor next week," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is expecting signs of a recovery but if figures do not sustain this view we could see a strong correction," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been on a slight uptrend since mid-April, buoyed by such expectations. \par \par \uc2  Despite the gains and Beijing's repeated "no-devaluation" pledge, there was no evidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan touched an intraday low of 8.2787 on Friday with most business done at 8.2785, they said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Thursday was 8.2786. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the Japanese yen at 6.8610 to 100 yen from Thursday's 6.8960. \par \par \uc2  It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0675 to one dollar. \par \par \uc2     ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5701hxf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
