\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up on foreign bank buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1999\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed firmer against the dollar in thin trade on Tuesday, buoyed by light demand from foreign banks that had approval to conduct local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  business, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2780 to one dollar compared with 8.2791 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "A few foreign banks designated to do local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  business bought the yuan today," said a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  "But their purchases were not that heavy and may have been just covering temporary shortages," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  China has so far approved 19 foreign banks for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  business in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the people's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the biggest member of the tightly controlled trading system. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly pledged to keep the yuan steady. \par \par \uc2  China's weakening trade picture, however, has put some pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Exports in the first quarter were down 7.9 percent from the same period of last year and the trade surplus narrowed sharply, official figures showed. \par \par \uc2     ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4k02q17\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\p