\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-China  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves up despite trade woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1999\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, April 13 (Reuters) - China announced on Tuesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by $1.67 billion in the first quarter of 1999 to $146.63 billion. \par \par \uc2  The reserves stood at $146.515 billion at the end of February and $145.090 billion at the end of January, the Financial News quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data as saying. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the steady increase in the reserves was in line with China's intensified crackdown on hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fraud. \par \par \uc2  "The crackdown has already showed a big impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," said an economist at the Bank of China, who declined to be identified. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are expected to show a slow but steady increase this year," he said. "Some firms have sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  they had been holding overseas to Chinese banks." \par \par \uc2  China's reserves, a key pillar of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose only $5.1 billion in 1998 despite a record trade surplus of $43.59 billion and foreign direct investment of $45.6 billion, according to earlier official data. \par \par \uc2  That compared with a surge of $34.9 billion in 1997. \par \par \uc2  Economists have forcast a relatively smaller trade surplus this year and smaller foreign investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  The reserves grew $730 million in the first quarter of last year but fell by $110 million in the second quarter due to capital flight sparked by worries the yuan would be devalued despite repeated insistence from the top that it would not be. \par \par \uc2  The downturn prompted Beijing to launch a nationwide crackdown on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fraud and ordered firms to send home hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegally held overseas. \par \par \uc2  That helped China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rise by $590 million in the third quarter and $3.9 billion in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  The steady rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves "has reflected boosted confidence in China's economy and its non-devaluation pledge", said a second economist at the Bank of China. \par \par \uc2  China's first quarter trade surplus plunged by 59.8 percent year on year to $4.28 billion, state media quoted customs figures as saying on Monday. \par \par \uc2  China's exports fell a year-on-year 7.9 percent to $37.27 billion in the first three months of this year, while imports surged 11.6 percent to $32.99 billion in the period. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible on the current account, mainly covering trade and services but the capital account, which covers investments, is largely closed. \par \par \uc2  In Shanghai, the yuan closed marginally higher against the dollar on Tuesday, shrugging off poor first quarter trade data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2796 to one dollar from 8.2797 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly controlled market to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The Financial News quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as saying China's gold reserves stood at 12.67 million ounces at the end of March, unchanged since the end of 1997. \par \par \uc2  ((Kevin Yao, Beijing Newsroom +8610 6532-1921, Fax +8610 6532-4978 beijing.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4d0375i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
