\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan edges up despite weak trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1999\par 06:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 13 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed marginally higher against the dollar on Tuesday, shrugging off poor first quarter trade data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2796 to one dollar from 8.2797 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  China's exports in the first quarter were down 7.9 percent from the same period of last year and the trade surplus narrowed sharply, official media said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly controlled market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The January-March trade surplus narrowed to $4.28 billion from $10.6 billion in the 1998 period. \par \par \uc2  "The data had been expected by the market and factored into the exchange rate," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that technical buying gave the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a bit of a boost, allowing it to record a second consecutive day of gains. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had been on a slight downward trend over the past few weeks as the market had expected China's foreign trade data to be weak in the first quarter, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had found strong support at 8.2800 despite the recent falls and was likely to move narrowly on the strong side of the key level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan hit an intraday high of 8.2795 on Tuesday and a low of 8.2799. Trade was dull with most business done at 8.2796. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2797. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the Japanese yen at 6.8563 to 100 yen from Monday's 6.8878. It ended lower against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0682 to one dollar from 1.0680. \par \par \uc2  ($1=8.28 yuan) \par \par \uc2  ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4d036y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
