\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Narrowly Weaker In Cautious Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 1999\par 06:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan (CNY) closed a touch weaker against the U.S. dollar Monday in lackluster trade. A holiday in international markets and domestic confidence in a stable yuan meant dealings were uneventful, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market movement was very slow today with most participants sidelined," said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  The U.S dollar closed Monday at CNY8.2795 from last Friday's CNY8.2794. It moved between CNY8.2790 and CNY8.2798 in thin trade valued at about $100 million. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Easter holiday, which has closed international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday through Monday, kept market participants sidelined Monday. \par \par \uc2  Trades made in China are cleared through New York. That means Monday's transactions won't be completed until Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the worsening situation in Kosovo, as NATO steps up military attacks, left Chinese traders cautious. \par \par \uc2  "The Kosovo situation is having a psychological impact on market participants, keeping traders cautious," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders added that confidence in the yuan remains solid, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is backed by healthy economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible under the current, or trade, account only. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supported by a large trade surplus, which reached $43 billion last year, and hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $146 billion. The central government has also pledged repeatedly not to devalue the yuan, despite more than a year of market rumors to the contrary. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent market fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Monday, the Hong Kong dollar closed unchanged at CNY1.0680 for the fourth straight day, while the yen closed at CNY6.8011 per 100 yen from CNY6.8500 last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Non-deliverable forward prices were unavailable Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Joshua Cherin; (8621)6218-3268; jcherin@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0408GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4502kel\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
