\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Slightly Higher On Dollar Demand For Imports \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 06:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan closed a touch stronger against the U.S. dollar Monday. Dollar buying from importers kept demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  high, but government-backed support for the yuan steadied the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S dollar closed Monday at CNY8.2799 from last Friday's 8.2800. It moved between CNY8.2795 and CNY8.2847 in thin trade valued at around $100 million. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yuan exchange to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a narrow trading band. The central government has pledged repeatedly not to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite more than a year of market rumors to the contrary. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they are confident that the yuan will remain at current levels. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar goes above CNY8.2800," said another dealer on the exchange floor. \par \par \uc2  Market participants tied dollar demand Monday to a pick up in projects requiring equipment imports, many from foreign-invested enterprises, a Shanghai-based trader with a state-owned commercial bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Yuan trading is based entirely on supply and demand from imports and exports," the Shanghai trader said. "Trade isn't influenced by international events or speculation." \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible under the current, or trade, account only. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supported by a large trade surplus, which reached $43 billion last year, and hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $146 billion. \par \par \uc2  The air strikes in Yugoslavia, which pushed the U.S. dollar higher in the international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, have had no impact on yuan trade, traders added. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Monday, the Hong Kong dollar closed unchanged at CNY1.0680, while the yen closed at CNY6.9053 per 100 yen from CNY6.9950 last Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the non-deliverable forwards market, money broker Exco Group in\par Singapore was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY8.4696 for delivery in six\par months and at CNY8.9796 over a one-year timeframe. The six month rate\par Monday carried a premium of CNY0.19, and the one-year rate CNY0.70.\par  -By Joshua Cherin; (8621)6218-3268; jcherin@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0450GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3t02eo2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
