o the government." \par \par \uc2  In other trading Wednesday, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0677 from CNY1.0678, while the Japanese yen closed at CNY7.0750 per Y100, up from CNY6.9750 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, non-deliverable forwards fell Wednesday, signaling firmer belief in the Chinese government's pledge not to devalue the yuan from overseas traders, who use the NDFs as a hedging tool. \par \par \uc2  In the NDF market, money broker Exco Group in Singapore was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY8.4892 for delivery in six months and at CNY8.9792 over a one-year timeframe. The six-month rate Wednesday carried a premium of CNY0.21 from CNY0.23 Tuesday and the one-year rate CNY0.70 from CNY0.78. \par \par \uc2  -By Joshua Cherin; (8621) 6218-3268; jcherin@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  24-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0420GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010824dv3o00bls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
