\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends down ahead of trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 1999\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed lower in thin trade on Monday amid speculation that the nation's foreign trade data for December due this week would be worse than expected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished the day at an inraday low of 8.2799 to one dollar from 8.2796 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market widely expects the December trade data would be worse than earlier estimates, that spurred some domestic bank traders to sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese government would post December and full year 1998 foreign trade data this week. \par \par \uc2  Despite Monday's fall, dealers said room for the yuan to fall further would be limited. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had approached the key support level of 8.2800 and traders widely expected that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local unit if it breached the level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In addition, a weak dollar on the world market did not support its further rises on the Shanghai market, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 110.47/50 against the Japanese yen in Tyoko by midday on Monday, down from 111.01/06 in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move narrowly just above the 8.2800 level in the next few days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Monday hit an intrady high of 8.2795 with most business done at 8.2797, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Friday was 8.2796. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed lower against the Japanese yen at 7.4900 to 100 Japanese yen from Friday's 7.4654. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0685 to one dollar at 1.0681. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1b06scp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
