\par\par \b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Slightly Higher On Technical Correction \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1999\par 05:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China's yuan finished slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, marking a technical correction after dollar buying emerged in previous sessions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed increased dollar selling to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to offset buying from state banks. \par \par \uc2  Traders said state banks were trying to meet domestic demand for dollars, as China's slowing sales overseas are likely to crimp earnings and hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows for Chinese exporters. Exporters are required to repatriate 85% of all overseas earnings. China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  predicted low to negative export growth in 1999. \par \par \uc2  China's exports last year reached $182 billion, the same as 1997. An economic slump in Asia has weakened regional demand for Chinese products. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar closed Wednesday at CNY8.2793, down from CNY8.2795 Tuesday. It traded between CNY8.2793 and CNY8.2800 in dealings of $150 million. China's yuan can be legally exchanged for trade in goods and services only. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expect more range-bound trade ahead of the Lunar New Year holiday in February. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0683, compared with the previous CNY1.0680, while the yen ended at CNY7.3999 per 100 yen, up from CNY7.3700. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, money broker Exco Group in Singapore was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY8.4989 for delivery in six months and at CNY8.9089 over a one-year timeframe. The six-month rate now carries a premium of CNY0.22, compared with CNY0.30 on Tuesday. The one-year premium is at CNY0.63, down a touch from CNY0.70. \par \par \uc2  -By Peter Wonacott; 8610 6532-6652; pwonacott@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0428GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv16002vw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
