\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese Yuan Ends Higher As Upward Pressure Continues \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 1998\par 05:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan came under renewed upward pressure Monday, ending a touch stronger on robust trade and capital-investment inflows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They noted the upward pressure is also the result of a sharp crackdown on illicit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows, which has sealed up China's leaky \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime and given new support to the yuan, which is still convertible under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or trade, account only. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Monday at CNY8.2777 from CNY8.2779 in the previous session. It traded in a range of CNY8.2776 and CNY8.2778, and dealings were thin at less than $200 million, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Faced with new upward pressure on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was actively watching the market Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from surging to a record high, traders said. They added they expect that trend to continue, as long as the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are enforced, and as long as China continues to see strong net capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Economists say they expect a net $60 billion to flow into China this year under both the trade and investment account. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0437GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dub900wxd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbl