\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese Yuan Strengthens As Capital Inflows Remain Healthy \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1998\par 05:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan strengthened a touch Wednesday, as strong capital inflows put moderate upward pressure on the local unit, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was monitoring trade closely, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yuan threatened to bounce higher by buying dollars. China's yuan is convertible under the current account only, or for trade-related purposes. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Wednesday at 8.2776 yuan (CNY). It closed the previous session at CNY8.2779, and traded in a range Wednesday of CNY8.2776-CNY8.2780. Participants said dealings were thinner than in previous sessions, though the exchange doesn't release daily volumes. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid to keep the yuan stable through a mix of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cracking down on illicit dollar purchases has left the market in balance" with light upward pressure, a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the semi-convertible yuan is likely to hover at present levels in the weeks ahead. \par \par \uc2  Large trade surpluses and huge foreign investment inflows have put continued upward pressure on the local unit in recent years. On Wednesday, traders said those same factors were at play, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and stem the yuan's rise. Economists say they expect net capital inflows into China to be worth about $60 billion this year. Most of those funds are converted into yuan, part of central government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rules. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0444GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dub400ra2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
