\par\par \b \uc2  China unveils sweeping reforms to  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1998\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, Oct 30 (Reuters) - China on Friday unveiled a sweeping reform package for its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to reduce risk and avoid the Asian financial contagion. \par \par \uc2  In the first official confirmation of the new structure for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , People's Bank of China deputy governor Liu Mingkang said the bank would set up nine regional branches to replace existing provincial branches. \par \par \uc2  The leaner structure would remove \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  branches from the sway of local officials, Liu wrote in an essay published in the China Economic Times. \par \par \uc2  "The scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current branch network is sprawling, their management hierarchy is complicated and the system is susceptible to local administrative \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also tighten supervision on foreign debt levels and the inflow of short-term capital in the wake of the Asian turmoil and the recent collapse of Guangdong International Trust and Investment Co (GITIC). \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month shut trust firm GITIC, a major borrower on international markets, for inability to pay maturing debt. \par \par \uc2  The revamp of the branch network was crucial to the health of China's financial system, Liu said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said Beijing aims to set up a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  along the lines of the U.S. Federal Reserve, giving the People's Bank more clout in the supervision of China's unruly financial sector. \par \par \uc2  Bankers have said the new branches would be located in the cities of Shenyang, Tianjin, Jinan, Nanjing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, Wuhan, Chengdu and Xian. \par \par \uc2  Liu said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the sole regulatory authority over commercial banks, surrendering its former responsibility for the insurance sector and the securities markets. \par \par \uc2  He urged China to take lessons from crisis-hit Asian countries, which he said were sunk by loose control of foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  "We should control the volume, structure and growth of foreign debt," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We should pay attention to improving the composition of foreign debt, paying particular heed to controlling the inflow of short-term capital." \par \par \uc2  Since the closure of GITIC, China's level of foreign debt has come under close scrutiny and Chinese officials have taken pains to underscore the government's ability to meet its foreign debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  China's State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday said outstanding foreign debt was $137.96 billion as of June 30, up $7.0 billion since the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  Liu said China must set up a mechanism to allow bankrupt financial institutions to go out of business and reject a system in which rescue measures would breed moral hazard. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duau05qds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
