\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan edges down, narrow movement seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 1998\par 06:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed marginally lower against the dollar on Wednesday, consolidating recent gains, and dealers said the local unit would move narrowly in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan edged down today on a consolidation after recent gains," a dealer said. "It moved narrowly for the entire session, and barring fresh factors this is likely to continue in the near term." \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished the day at 8.2779 to one dollar from 8.2777 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was buoyed recently by China's crackdown on foriegn exchange irregularities and the rebound in the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The recently narrow trading range for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be in line with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a number of occasions in August and September to prevent sharp swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dual02b1f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
