\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends at record closing high vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 1998\par 06:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 12 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan ended at a record closing high against the dollar on Monday, aided by strong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves announced last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2774 to the dollar, erasing the former peak close of 8.2777 set on Friday. Dealers said the recent gains of the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and Beijing's crackdown on illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities, also contributed to the yuan's rise. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $141.1 billion as of the end of September, up $1.2 billion from the start of this year, the official Xinhua news agency said. \par \par \uc2  "The data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were still high," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the slight rise in the reserves also pointed to reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Signs of less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged bank traders to increase their positions," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment towards the local unit improved as a result of the yen's rise and Beijing's expanded controls on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  use. \par \par \uc2  The yen stood at 115.85/95 to one dollar by midday in Tokyo, compared with 116.30/40 in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  China has ordered domestic companies which had bought \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with falsified documents to return the funds, giving them a brief grace period. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move on the strong side of the 8.2780 level on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan traded between a high of 8.2772 and a low of 8.2778. Trade was active with most business done at 8.2775, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2777. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at a new 1998 low of 7.1206 to 100 yen from the former low of 7.0075 set on Friday. It ended nearly unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0674 to one dollar from 1.0673. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duac01nlz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
