\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese Yuan Ends -2: PBOC Sold Yuan To Slow Rising Trend \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1998\par 05:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan ended unchanged at its highest point this year against the U.S. dollar Friday as Beijing's crackdown on illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading continued to stifle demand for dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  yuan sales pulled the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a little lower during the session, but failed to stop it rising again at the close of trading. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan will get stronger and stronger" if the "PBOC doesn't hold it steady" by selling yuan for dollars, a Agricultural Bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China doesn't want the yuan to strengthen too much against the dollar, because a stronger yuan makes China's exports more expensive. Export growth is already slowing as demand from crisis-hit Asian neighbors weakens, and China's export competitiveness is cut because of other regional devaluations. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the U.S. dollar closed unchanged from Thursday at CNY8.2777. It traded between CNY8.2780 and CNY8.2775, with most transactions contracted around CNY8.2776 and CNY8.2777, traders said. \par \par \uc2  According to other market participants, dollar trading - which usually comprises around 95% of all trades - slimmed back a touch Friday, with investors shifting some attention to the yen. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at a year high of CNY7.0100 per Y100, following its recent rally against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on global markets. \par \par \uc2  "Investors were paying more attention to the yen," said one trader. He noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has dominated trading on the Shanghai-based exchange since the exchange opened in 1994, allowed the yen to trade freely against \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's semi-convertible yuan. \par \par \uc2  "The PBOC doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yen deals," he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0344GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dua90016w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
