\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan at record high close on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  curbs. \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan ended at a record closing high of 8.2777 to the dollar on Thursday, buoyed by Beijing's recent measures tightening \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The close was the highest since the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, the national interbank market, was set up in April 1994 after a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  realignment. \par \par \uc2  It erased the former record of 8.2779 set on April 30 this year and was up from Wednesday's 8.2780 closing level. \par \par \uc2  The State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered companies which had used falsified documents to purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from state banks to return the funds, official media reported after the market closed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  It would reduce penalties for companies that complied within two days, according to the reports. \par \par \uc2  "The latest request coupled with previous measures to tighten exchange controlso positive sentiment towards the yuan," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Beijing previously had ordered domestic companies to send back foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held illegally overseas before October 1. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the measures, targeted at \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegally retained by local firms for hedging against a possible devaluation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would bring more dollars onto the market and in turn boost the yuan. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to slow the yuan's rise, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan's advance was registered in thin trade. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to see a correction on Friday but it still had room to rise in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Thursday opened higher at 8.2776, hitting an intraday peak of 8.2765 and a low of 8.2779. Most trade was at 8.2777, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2778. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at an intraday low of 6.8170 to 100 yen from 6.3350. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0673 to one dollar. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua801gkt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
