\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan edges up, equals record closing high. \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 1998\par 06:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan ended slightly firmer against the dollar on Tuesday, equalling its closing high set in April, after a senior official re-affirmed Beijing's pledge not to devalue, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2779 to one dollar, matching the post-1994 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  realignment peak, and up from Monday's 8.2781. \par \par \uc2  Minister of Finance Xiang Huaicheng, in Washington for the IMF annual meeting, was quoted by local newspapers as saying that China would not devalue the yuan. \par \par \uc2  "Xiang's remarks gave the yuan further support as sentiment improved after gains over the past two weeks," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had advanced smartly over the last two weeks, buoyed by Beijing's recent crackdown on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  irregularities. The campaign was expected to bring more dollars onto the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the dollar but fears of such action kept trade cautious, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "As the yuan is now at the record closing high level, concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have begun to mount and that capped the yuan's rise today," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market over the last few months to keep the yuan from rising or falling too quickly. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to see a correction on Wednesday barring fresh positive factors. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan moved in a tight range between an intraday low of 8.2781 and a high of 8.2778. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2780. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.1850 to 100 yen from 6.1121. It ended little changed against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0672 to one dollar from 1.0673. \par \par \uc2     - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua601br7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
