\par\par \b \uc2  Chinese Yuan Ends -3: Black Mkt Rate Remains At CNY9.02 \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 1998\par 06:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Sentiment in the stability of the yuan has been weakened in recent months by concerns that sluggish foreign investment and a downturn in export growth could pressure China to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Companies in China that are able to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been trying to hedge against a possible decline in the value of the yuan. \par \par \uc2  However, the number of Chinese companies and individuals permitted to trade yuan for dollars remains a small part of the country's economy. The crackdown on prohibited dollar purchases has lightened buying pressure on the official exchange, allowing China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to maintain current rates without market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. \par \par \uc2  "Because there are few dollar buying orders, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is much quieter than earlier this year," another trader said. \par \par \uc2  The PBOC has dominated trade on Shanghai's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange since the exchange was established in 1994. \par \par \uc2  China's move to stamp out illegal exchange-based trading comes in step with an attack on black market transactions. Friday, black market traders were buying dollars for CNY9.02, unchanged from Tuesday. The rate was driven up from CNY8.83 two weeks ago by stricter policing of illegal swaps. Tighter law enforcement is now threatening to put black marketeers in jail. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Friday, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0672 from CNY1.0671. The yen ended at CNY6.1000 per 100 yen from CNY6.0600. The two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  account for only about 5% of daily transactions. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, which shows how much participants are willing to pay for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a specific maturity in the future, money broker Exco Group in Singapore Friday was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY8.6683 for delivery in six months and at CNY9.1283 over a one-year timeframe. \par \par \uc2  -By Joshua Cherin; (8621)6218-3268; jcherin@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  25-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0422GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du9p00uj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
