\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up on tighter  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  controls. \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1998\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed higher against the dollar in active trade on Wednesday after Beijing renewed its pledge to crack down on illegal foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2783 to one dollar from 8.2786 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Beijing would implement a series of measures, including a nationwide inspection of financial institutions and trading firms, to check irregularities. The plan was reported on state television after the market closed on Tuesday and carried in major newspapers on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the tighter controls would make local banks more cautious in buying dollars and that would translate into a surplus of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment towards the yuan was strengthened due to the renewed pledge on tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there no signs that the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to check the yuan's rise on Wednesday as it did on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had recently been selling yuan to unwind positions it built up in August when it built up positions to keep the local unit above the 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market of late to keep trading of the yuan steady and prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from moving sharply in either direction, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan would meet near-term resistance at 8.2779, the record closing high for the yuan against the dollar set on April 30. A correction was expected on Thursday after gains recorded over the past four days. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened lower at 8.2790, hitting an intraday low of 8.2794 early in the session and a high of 8.2782 in late trade. \par \par \uc2  Most business was done at 8.2785, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2785. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.1502 to 100 yen from 6.2121. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0680 to one dollar from 1.0678. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9g016n9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
