\par\par \b \uc2  China  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market turnover edges up in August. \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 1998\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Turnover on China's official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was equivalent to $4.412 billion in August, up slightly from $4.154 billion in July, the Business News said on Saturday, quoting exchange figures. \par \par \uc2  The Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market trades U.S. dollars, Hong Kong dollars and the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The total turnover in August included US$3.959 billion, HK$1.09 billion and 6.167 billion Japanese yen, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan was little changed at 8.2800 to the U.S. dollar at the end of August from 8.2799 at the end of July, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yuan was under heavy downward pressure in recent weeks due to the weakness of the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and China's slowing economy. \par \par \uc2  But the yuan was supported by Beijing's repeated pledges not to devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market several times in August to keep the yuan steady at around the 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was down at 5.8146 per 100 Japanese yen at the end of August from 5.7627 at the end of July, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  It edged down to 1.0687 per Hong Kong dollar in August from 1.0681 the month earlier, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  ($1=8.28 yuan) \par \par \uc2  