\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance:Nikkei Nears 12-Yr Lows, Falls 2.2% \b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 11:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- The Nikkei Stock Average neared 12-year lows as concerns about the economy and banking problems continued to grip investors; the Nikkei ended down 329.27 points, or 2.2%, at 14,794.66. \par \par \uc2  -- Shares of Japan's seven trust banks were all weaker, with four of them hitting new year-to-date lows and one matching its 1998 low; the steep declines came after Fitch IBCA downgraded long-term ratings on five Japanese trust banks last Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Plummeting Japanese stock prices boosted the dollar against the yen in late Asian trading despite persistent market concerns about the potential for yen-supportive action by Japanese monetary authorities; Russia's announcement of new capital controls and a ruble devaluation also pushed the dollar up against the mark; however, early in European trading at 0830 GMT, the dollar was at Y146.20, compared with Y146.30 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuroda, head of the International Bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , repeated warnings about the yen's weakness against the dollar, saying that Japan will take appropriate steps when necessary. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore shares ended 2.3% lower, extending last week's precipitous decline, dealers said. ; Taiwan shares ended 1.4% lower as investors were worried about the slowing economy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  -- Japan's main opposition party extended an olive branch to the government, saying it is willing to compromise to push crucial banking reform legislation through Parliament. \par \par \uc2  -- Japanese Prime Minister Obuchi said while he understands that the nation's rock-bottom official discount rate of 0.5% was a heavy burden for pensioners, it benefits the economy by encouraging corporate spending and housing investment. \par \par \uc2  -- The average value of land in Japan on Jan. 1, based on assessments used to determine inheritance and gift taxes, was 5.0% lower year on year at Y170,000 per square meter, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong has launched an international campaign to explain and justify last week's first-ever \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local stock market, the South \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Morning Post reported. \par \par \uc2  -- South Korea's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to an all-time high of $43.91 billion on Aug. 15, up from $43.02 billion at the end of July, the Bank of Korea reported. \par \par \uc2  -- Total securities tax paid on transactions on the Taiwan Stock Exchange during the first seven months of the year tumbled 13.4% to NT$63.7 billion, Taiwan's cabinet reported. \par \par \uc2  -- Indonesian banking authorities are preparing to make the owners of three of the nation's largest banks, including the closest business associate of former President Suharto, repay US$7 billion in government bailout loans. \par \par \uc2  -- Renewing his attack on hedge funds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, Malaysia Finance Minister Anwar said the international financial system should be subject to disclosure and transparency rules, if the same is expected of Asian economies. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0917GMT \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8h07025\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
