\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends firmer, aided by trade data. \b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 06:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly higher against the dollar on Tuesday, buoyed by better-than-expected trade data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China's exports rose by a year-on-year 6.9 percent in the first seven months to reach $103.1 billion, the official Xinhua news agency reported late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The trade data were encouraging, taking into consideration the prolonged Asian financial crisis," a dealer said. "They gave the local unit strong support today." \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2797 to one dollar on Tuesday from 8.2800 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the gains, dealers said selling pressure was heavy around the key 8.2800 level due to the continued weakness of the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The yen was down slightly at 146.37/40 by midday in Tokyo from 146.23/33 in late New York on Monday after moving narrowly throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan would also gain further support on Wednesday from remarks by Liu Mingkang, deputy governor of the People's Bank of China, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that China had no reason to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The remarks were too late to affect trade today. \par \par \uc2  "The renminbi (yuan) does not need to be devalued and will not be devalued," Liu told a news conference in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  Liu told reporters that a minor devaluation would not aid China's exports while it would deal a severe blow to other economies in the region. \par \par \uc2  Liu also warned foreign and domestic interests about excessive speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While he did not elaborate on the remarks, his statement was seen as one of Beijing's strongest against speculation on the possibility of devaluation of the yuan. They added that the statement would help stabilise trading in the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Speculation on a devaluation had pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a five-year low of 9.3 to one dollar on Shanghai's black market last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has since recovered to around 8.7 on the black market. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has repeatedly vowed not to devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 China Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, the Shanghai-based interbank market, in recent weeks to defend the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying helped prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, holding it at the 8.2800 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to hold to the strong side of the key level on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2800 on Tuesday, hitting an intraday high of 8.2795 and a low of 8.2849. Trading was active with most business done at 8.2799, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed little changed against the Japanese yen at 5.6410 to 100 yen from 5.6503. It ended almost unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0689 to one dollar from 1.0690. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8b02v9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
