\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards climb by midday, market cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 07:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab      Midday\tab      Open\tab      Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT   7.7487/97\tab   7.7475/85\tab 7.7465/75\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2   3-Month    1,150-1,200     1,080-1,150    1,025-1,075 \par \par \uc2   6-Month    2,500-2,600     2,200-2,300    2,100-2,300 \par \par \uc2   1-Year     5,000-5,200     4,750-4,950    4,500-4,800 \par \par \uc2  INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Overnight  7.00-8.00\tab  7.50-8.00\tab 7.00-8.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  3-Month    11.20-11.70     10.70-11.25    10.60-11.12\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  6-Month    11.50-12.00     11.00-11.68    11.10-12.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  1-Year     11.50-12.00     11.00-12.00    11.70-12.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 11 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards climbed by Tuesday's midday after a sharp fall in Hong Kong's stock market spurred nervousness in the money markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The blue-chip Hang Seng Index fell through the key 7,000 support level to a five-year low of 6,889 by late morning and continued dropping.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Money market sentiment was not panicky but remained cautious on fears that speculators might stage another attack on the Hong Kong dollar following last week's three-day salvo, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said trading was quite thin by midsession on Tuesday, exaggerating moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the scale of the Hong Kong dollar short sales was much smaller than last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Forwards trading volume was rather thin today, though they remained well-supported at current levels," a chief dealer at a major European bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "So a few major transactions could help push up forward rates almost immediately," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Three-month forwards climbed by over 100 points during midsession, compared with some 200 points by midsession last Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The six-month and one-year jumped by 400-500 points respectively, indicating that buying interest was more concentrated at the longer end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Market attention today is on the longer end of the yield curve," another dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Movement in longer-dated rates has been directing trade over the past few months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was heard offering overnight and three-month term money into the interbank market, helping to keep rates soft at the short end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But rates continued to hold firm across the board.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the underlying tone for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was weak, with the dollar/yen rate marching closer to 150 weighing on sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Worries over the possible devaluation of the Chinese yuan in the near term temporarily abated on Tuesday on the back of repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Chinese government over the past week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tightly controlled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Monday, its third move in a little over a week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The deputy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Liu Mingkang said the bank would take necessary steps to maintain the yuan's stability and advised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculators "not to miscalculate".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8b02ufe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
