\par\par \b \uc2  Pressure abates on Hong Kong dollar, shares bounce. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Angi Li Yeung \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 12:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interest rates and \par \par \uc2  forward rates eased on Monday as pressure on the local dollar \par \par \uc2  abated, giving a lift to the territory's battered stock market. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the mood was brighter after the weekend passed \par \par \uc2  without signs of further speculative attacks against the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Hong Kong dollar had been under heavy selling \par \par \uc2  pressure from overseas funds starting on Wednesday last week. \par \par \uc2      "As nothing happened over the weekend, after most expected \par \par \uc2  something would, market sentiment improved markedly today," one \par \par \uc2  money market dealer said. \par \par \uc2      Forward and interest rates opened weaker in Hong Kong and \par \par \uc2  continued to soften throughout the day on continuous offers by \par \par \uc2  major local banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate \par \par \uc2  was at 11.01 percent at the 0330 GMT fixing, down from 12.69 \par \par \uc2  percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said Hong Kong banks had maintained a prudent \par \par \uc2  liquidity management policy since last October's massive \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attack and thus were better prepared to handle last \par \par \uc2  week's assault. \par \par \uc2      Indeed, local banks with large Hong Kong dollar deposit \par \par \uc2  bases took advantage of higher interest rates to lend, they \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said the market remained nervous, with the \par \par \uc2  Japanese yen still weak and China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under threat as \par \par \uc2  well. \par \par \uc2      "Though the market sentiment moderately improved today, most \par \par \uc2  of us remain cautious because the war is not over yet," said \par \par \uc2  another dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets \par \par \uc2  again on Monday, keeping the yuan at 8.28 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2      On Sunday, China's President Jiang Zemin told Japanese \par \par \uc2  Foreign Minister Masahiko Komura Beijing was determined to avoid \par \par \uc2  devaluing the yuan despite a slowing economy. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong residents appeared mostly unperturbed by last \par \par \uc2  week's salvo against the Hong Kong dollar. Several local banks \par \par \uc2  said there was no appreciable switching from Hong Kong dollar \par \par \uc2  deposits into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated deposits. \par \par \uc2  "There is no noticeable change in the overall mix of \par \par \uc2  clients' deposits over the past week," a spokesman for Hongkong \par \par \uc2  and Shanghai Banking Corp said. \par \par \uc2  Hang Seng Bank, one of the largest local banks, said it saw \par \par \uc2  a slight increase in U.S. dollar deposits by both individual and \par \par \uc2  institutional customers last week, while Hong Kong dollar \par \par \uc2  deposits remained stable. \par \par \uc2  On Saturday, Hong Kong Financial Secretary Donald Tsang said \par \par \uc2  speculators could not succeed as long as Hong Kong people \par \par \uc2  supported the government's policy of maintaining the peg. \par \par \uc2      "If Hong Kong people support Hong Kong's present policy, I \par \par \uc2  think the speculators will lose money," said Tsang. \par \par \uc2      The Hong Kong dollar has been pegged to the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  since 1983 at a rate of HK$7.8 per US$1 and is permitted to \par \par \uc2  float in a narrow range around that level. It closed at \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7466/76 per U.S. dollar on Monday, firmer than Friday's \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7495/05 close. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits already make up a significant \par \par \uc2  share of deposits in Hong Kong financial institutions. In 1997, \par \par \uc2  42 percent of bank deposits were denominated in foreign \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong stocks ended slightly higher in choppy Monday \par \par \uc2  trade on easier local interest rates, but brokers said gains \par \par \uc2  were limited because investors were worried about a weakening \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen toyed with its eight-year low of 146.75 per U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar but managed to stay above that level during Asian trading \par \par \uc2  hours. But dealers said the outlook for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  was bleak. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's blue-chip Hang Seng Index rose 16.21 points, or \par \par \uc2  0.23 percent, to close at 7,034.62. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02tvi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
