\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market to support yuan. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 10 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waded into the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears that Beijing may devalue the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China bought the local unit in the tightly controlled market to hold the yuan at 8.2800 to the U.S. dollar, the third time since July 31 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to hold the yuan at the 8.2800 level," one local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been pressured by the sagging Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finish above the key 8.2800 level for the past few weeks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was no indication of the volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan buying on Monday, but dealers said trading overall was light. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the People's Bank in Beijing declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The move helped the yuan close at 8.2800 to one dollar, little changed from the 8.2799 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to defend the 8.2800 mark and a fall below that key level could indicate a shift in policy. \par \par \uc2  State banks also bought the yuan after Chinese President Jiang Zemin told Japanese Foreign Minister Masahiko Komura on Sunday that Beijing was determined to avoid devaluing the yuan despite a slowing economy, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The pledge helped boost confidence among domestic banks that the yuan was not likely to be devalued, at least for the time being," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  China's top leaders have vowed repeatedly to keep the yuan stable, since a devaluation could spark a new round of falls in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and impact the world economy. \par \par \uc2  But they have also hinted that Beijing's will to resist a devaluation would depend on Japan's ability to keep the yen from depreciating further. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was steady at around 146 yen in Tokyo at midday, near eight-year highs. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02szq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
