\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  c. bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , yuan little changed. \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the Chinese yuan at 8.2800 to the dollar at the close on Monday, little changed from Friday's final level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the yuan slipped below the key level in late morning trade but buying by the People's Bank of China, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , brought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to its 8.2800 finish. That compared with 8.2799 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to hold the yuan at the 8.2800 level," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said other state banks also bought the yuan after President Jiang Zemin on Sunday repeated Beijing's pledge not to devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The renewed pledge helped boost confidence among domestic banks that the yuan was not likely to be devalued at least for the time being," a second dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Buying by domestic banks was active at 8.2800," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan stable recently. There was no indication of the volume of its buying on Monday but trading overall was light. \par \par \uc2  The yuan's weighted average price on Friday was 8.2801, officials said on Monday. That reflected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Despite domestic support, the yuan was pressured on Monday by renewed falls of the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yen was at 146.18/28 to one dollar by midday in Tokyo, nearing the 1998 low of 146.75. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a narrow narrow range between an intraday high of 8.2798 and 8.2800 for most of the session, though it hit a low of 8.2849 in late morning. Most business was done at 8.2799, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the yen at 5.6503 to 100 yen from 5.7199. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0690 to one dollar from 1.0683. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02smh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
